WEBVTT

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.600
Next up is today's forecast.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.850
Many places throughout the country
will have record cold temperatures.

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:29.360
"Together with Maman | MV Shoot
Kujukuri Beach, Chiba"

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:29.360
Some areas will be below zero.
So, when you go out...

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:34.570
Well... Okay, then! Good morning!

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:39.870
The music video we're shooting today
will be used in the summer,

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:44.710
but the videographer seems particular
about things and wants to take time.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:46.460
I-It's cold!

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:50.460
So... we're moving it up
and shooting it today.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:54.880
The title of the song is
"Long, Hot Summer."

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:58.640
Act like you're having a blast
in the summer. I'm counting on you!

00:00:58.680 --> 00:00:59.970
"Episode 4: Long, Hot Summer"

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:04.020
"Episode 4: Long, Hot Summer"

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:04.020
Okay, then! Let's start now!

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:08.060
Express the feeling of the music
using your whole body.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:11.150
Like, "Wow, it's so hot!"

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.400
Ah... It's cold.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:21.330
Well, I've never been happier about
wearing a costume than today's shoot.

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:24.290
Wearing a tank top?
That's pretty much a form of torture.

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:25.120
Whoa!

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:30.380
Ahhh! Cold! Cold! Please don't
stick your hand in the gap! Ahh! Ahh!

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:32.920
Ahh! I can't bear it! I can't bear it!

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:36.590
Well, I'm sorry, Uramichi-kun!

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:41.600
It looks like today's shoot is going to be
tough because of the decisions we made.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:43.100
It's not tough at all.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:46.060
Oh... is that right?

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:47.310
Aren't you cold?

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:49.690
No, not at all.

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:50.230
--Honestly, are you really not cold?

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:52.270
--Uramichi Oniisan is incredible.
--Honestly, are you really not cold?

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:53.530
--Uramichi Oniisan is incredible.
--Yeah, not at all.

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:54.480
--I thought I'd been training
well in my own way.
--Yeah, not at all.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.700
--I thought I'd been training
well in my own way.
--Really? Honestly? You're not lying?

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:57.610
--But maybe I don't have
enough muscle... I feel cold.
--Really? Honestly? You're not lying?

00:01:57.610 --> 00:01:59.360
--But maybe I don't have
enough muscle... I feel cold.
--Yeah, not at all.

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:04.040
No, any way you look at it,
even Uramichi-san should be feeling cold.

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:06.500
He's being stubborn
for who knows what reason.

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:09.830
--His hand was as cold as ice.
--Are you really, really, really not cold?

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:10.750
--I'm not cold at all.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:14.000
--If you look closely,
his skin's full of goose bumps.
--I'm not cold at all.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:20.300
The ocean is vast...

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:24.520
See? His vocabulary has hit
rock bottom due to the cold.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:27.560
Uramichi Oniisan.

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:33.320
First, we'd like to shoot you busting open
a watermelon, a summer staple.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:36.070
But watermelons are not
for sale this time of year.

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:37.570
I can imagine.

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:39.320
I only found a winter gourd.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:41.240
"Winter Gourd"

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:41.240
Winter... gourd!

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:44.870
"BOLD
Muckee"

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:44.870
If we draw wavy lines on it,
it'll look just fine.

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:47.330
--Squeak, squeak, squeak!
--Whoa...

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:49.500
It's a watermelon. Watermelon!

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.380
Err... It's cold.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:55.050
Hm?

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:55.800
--It's a watermelon any way you look at it.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.670
--Hm? What?
--It's a watermelon any way you look at it.

00:02:57.670 --> 00:02:59.260
--What is it?
--It's a watermelon any way you look at it.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:02.390
Say “How about I bust your head open?”

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:04.560
Oh, okay. How about I bust your head--

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:08.060
Hold on a sec. That'll get you fired.

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:11.850
To start with, it's physically
impossible because it's too hard.

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:14.690
I've been wondering all this time,
but what's that costume?

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:17.030
The sun spirit.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:21.240
Now, now. A winter gourd
is like a raw egg...

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:23.740
...in the hands of our ace.

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:26.620
Training is just about
the only thing the man can do.

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:29.500
How about I bust your head open?

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:30.500
I'm sorry!

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:35.250
Ahhh! This is a program
for hardcore sadists

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:38.460
masquerading as an educational show!

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:39.970
Clench your teeth.

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:43.390
Hey! You were going to hit me
instead of the watermelon from the start!

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:49.470
Stop it! Don't act like I'm already dead!

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:50.180
"Watermelon Busting"

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:54.150
"Watermelon Busting"

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:54.150
Okay, that's enough mourning.
We'll start shooting now!

00:03:56.770 --> 00:03:59.190
Go left! Left...! More left!

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:00.070
Left!

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:03.070
How come you guys are suddenly
working so well together now?!

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.120
Smash! Smash!

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:15.080
Understand that you just escaped death.

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:17.500
"Creak"

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:17.500
Understand that you just escaped death.

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:23.010
Since they're cutting the audio, he's
smiling while he says that. It's scary!

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:25.260
Okay! Next is the scene
for the song's chorus,

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:29.220
the "I lost sight of the mosquito,
and now I can't get to sleep" part.

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:31.180
Since we came all the way
to shoot at a beach,

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:35.900
I'd like to see the mood of "I'm really
having fun playing on the beach!"

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:39.020
You know, that thing you see
all the time. You splash each other

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:42.030
and go "tee-hee-hee!" and "ha, ha, ha!"

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:45.950
I want to shoot that, so I want you
to splash water on each other.

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:50.120
Long, Hot Summer!

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:54.250
"Splash water"

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:54.250
Okay, guys! Now that you're
done changing clothes,

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:56.250
"Splash water"

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:56.250
we'll start shooting again!

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:01.340
Hey, shut up!

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:04.800
Don't say "It's cold," "I wanna
go home," or "I wanna quit"!

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:07.390
I haven't said anything yet.

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:11.770
Well then, Usa-Kuma-san.
Please take these water guns.

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:14.730
What? <i>We </i>are going to do it?!

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:17.860
What do we do? What do we do?
He's gonna kill us.

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:19.730
It'll be fine if we don't hit him.

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:25.030
Whoa, cool! He's not getting
even a drop of water on him,

00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:27.990
but it looks like Kumao is spraying him.

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:31.200
This was the first time he could put his
full concentration and fine motor control,

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:34.660
which he trained in the Japanese
archery club while in college,

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:37.250
to good use in this job.

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:41.130
O... Okay...

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:43.170
I'm dead meat if I hit him...

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:45.130
I'm dead meat if I hit him...

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:48.140
I'm dead meat if I hit him...!

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:49.010
Take this!

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:51.720
Ah...

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:59.270
On the other hand, all his high jump
training with the track and field club

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:05.030
from his college days
was of no use at all.

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:10.240
After this, the shoot went on with
one thing happening after another.

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:13.290
I can't see in front of me.

00:06:17.790 --> 00:06:21.210
Okay, the sun is down
and the atmosphere is nice,

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:25.960
so we'll shoot a scene where
you look up at fireworks in yukata.

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:29.930
But naturally, we couldn't get
the budget to shoot off fireworks,

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:33.260
so we'll add them later on using CG.

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:37.770
Then why didn't you just make
everything CG from the start?

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:43.110
Try acting as if you're having fun
watching fireworks go off.

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:50.820
Hmm...

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:55.700
"Fireworks"

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:55.700
It still doesn't look like
there are fireworks.

00:06:55.700 --> 00:07:01.120
You guys are pros, right?! I don't believe
that you're looking at fireworks!

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:06.460
Use your facial expressions more
to show that it's summer!

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:08.800
No, no! Not good enough!

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:10.380
More!

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:12.140
More!

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:13.970
Yay!

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:16.180
Okay, that's good!

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:18.810
The shoot is complete!

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:20.520
Thank you for your good work!

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:21.770
That was cold, wasn't it?

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:23.730
--I'm going to the public bath.
--Hm?

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:30.650
Hey! U-UFO! I saw a UFO!

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:34.780
Oh, boy. It's so cold
that Iketeru is hallucinating.

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:36.370
I swear it's true!

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:46.170
"Iketeru Daga"

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:53.340
Err... Um, I'm sorry...
for causing you so much trouble.

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:57.350
I have to set a good example for children.

00:07:57.350 --> 00:08:00.310
To think that I can't properly manage
my own physical condition...

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:03.400
I don't deserve to be
called a singer Oniisan.

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:06.520
Ah, hey! Sayuri-san!

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:09.570
Stop it. I'm discussing
something important.

00:08:09.570 --> 00:08:12.400
Sayuri-san! It tickles!

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:15.950
Okay! Iketeru-kun got a cold
and is out today,

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:19.620
so we'll change some parts
of today's recording.

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:21.500
Who's Sayuri-san?

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:22.830
His dog.

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:26.670
We're thinking of not hiding
that Iketeru-kun is out today

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:29.880
and trying to incorporate this situation
into today's show structure.

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:32.720
Well, instead of shooting
a full-length show,

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:35.970
why don't you combine the existing
videos and music videos to fudge it?

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:38.390
<i>Together with Maman</i>
without Iketeru Oniisan?!

00:08:38.390 --> 00:08:42.180
It'll be sad if it somehow
works out okay, right?!

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:45.190
Hm?

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:53.070
This is a good opportunity to teach
children how important everyone is.

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:56.240
That each one of us is
an absolutely necessary...

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:58.910
...and precious existence!

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:06.080
That's our Utano-chan!
What a great sentiment!

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:10.130
Iketeru Oniisan. What wonderful
co-workers you've got.

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:11.210
What?

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:13.800
I'm sorry. I wasn't listening.

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:15.050
"Iketeru Daga"

00:09:15.050 --> 00:09:17.260
"Iketeru Daga"

00:09:15.050 --> 00:09:17.260
Hey! Sayuri-san!

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:18.680
"Together with Maman"

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:21.100
Hello, kids!

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:23.140
How are you?!

00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:32.280
Where's Iketeru Oniisan?

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:35.990
Iketeru Oniisan has gone
someplace kinda far away,

00:09:35.990 --> 00:09:38.950
but his heart is always with you.

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:42.410
Hey, Utano Oneesan.
That gives the wrong impression.

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:45.410
Is Iketeru Oniisan gone?

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:47.210
He finally got fired?

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:48.920
I feel bad.

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:52.670
It's natural for a normal human being
to get sick if they are out on the beach

00:09:52.670 --> 00:09:56.220
all day long, half-naked,
in the middle of winter.

00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:57.720
What about Uramichi-san?

00:09:57.720 --> 00:10:02.220
He is a gorilla wearing
a good-looking-guy mask.

00:10:05.430 --> 00:10:09.020
Sayuri-san, give me the blanket back.

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:12.480
Darn... I feel cold.

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:14.190
I'm gonna die...

00:10:15.740 --> 00:10:19.990
Iketeru. I made porridge, so have some.

00:10:19.990 --> 00:10:21.280
Thanks.

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:28.040
Waaah! It hurts, hop. It hurts, hop.

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:29.960
What happened, Usao-kun?!

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:33.630
I fell and hurt myself, so the
wound will get infected, hop!

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:35.420
This is really bad, hop!

00:10:35.420 --> 00:10:36.920
Are you okay?

00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:39.130
Poor thing.

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:41.090
This is a job for...

00:10:41.090 --> 00:10:43.220
...Jerminator!

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:48.230
Ah! That voice...!

00:10:48.230 --> 00:10:51.150
Jerminator won't save you today!

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:52.610
It's because...

00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:57.490
...I, Bacterian, beat him
with a cold bacterium!

00:10:57.490 --> 00:10:58.490
What?!

00:10:58.490 --> 00:11:01.910
What a villain you are, <i>kuma</i>!

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:04.620
Say whatever you want.

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:06.830
You darn stupid bunny.

00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:08.000
What?

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:10.920
You're in this situation
because you badmouth a lot,

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:12.500
for example, calling me a gorilla...

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:15.500
What? No way! He heard it?

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:16.880
Ow, ow, ow...

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:19.260
Don't pinch my cheek through the gap!

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:20.880
Ow, ow, ow...

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:26.970
Oh, no! If we don't do something,
the Earth will be eroded by Bacterian!

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:30.270
But I wonder why...

00:11:30.270 --> 00:11:34.270
I don't have fun even when I do
bad things if he's not around.

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:36.650
Bacterian...

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:42.660
Maybe it's because I want someone
to stop me that I keep doing bad things.

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:44.240
What an attention hog.

00:11:44.240 --> 00:11:46.370
He sounds like a pain.

00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:50.460
I bid you farewell until the day
I can fight him fair and square!

00:12:01.550 --> 00:12:04.300
Kids! Don't become
a coward like Bacterian,

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:10.270
who only sticks to his principles
because he's obsessed with something.

00:12:10.270 --> 00:12:13.190
If your goal is just
to compete with someone,

00:12:13.190 --> 00:12:17.570
you can never become
better than that person.

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:19.570
Is Bacterian no good?

00:12:19.570 --> 00:12:20.990
He's no good!

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:24.820
As long as he's obsessed with Jerminator,
he can't conquer the Earth!

00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:26.160
He said it straight.

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:28.080
How ruthless.

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:30.200
Remember that you can't aim high

00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:33.830
while making friends
or being afraid of loneliness.

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:37.880
That thinking's the reason
he's spectacularly single, isn't it?

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:39.550
Right, Usao-kun?!

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:41.510
Yes, sir!

00:12:41.510 --> 00:12:43.180
Uramichi Oniisan!

00:12:44.180 --> 00:12:47.390
Here. Let's wipe your feet
real clean. Okay, Sayuri-san?

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:50.970
Iketeru.

00:12:56.520 --> 00:13:00.690
I bought some jelly and stuff
for you when I took a walk.

00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:01.940
Okay.

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:05.320
I dreamed about my childhood.

00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:11.370
Of all the things, it was about when I had
a fever on the day of the piano recital.

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:14.620
What? Sorry, I wasn't listening.

00:13:17.210 --> 00:13:21.550
If you come too close to me,
you'll catch my cold... Sis...

00:13:21.550 --> 00:13:23.470
"Izakaya"            "Yakitori"
"Karaage"
"Open"

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:28.050
I wonder if Iketeru-kun is frail.

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:31.430
I heard that he tends to get fevers
easily, ever since he was a child.

00:13:31.430 --> 00:13:33.730
Ah, so he really is.

00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:38.400
But he said he lives with his older
sister now, so he's probably okay.

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:40.360
You sure know a lot about him.

00:13:40.360 --> 00:13:42.230
His sister is a musician.

00:13:42.230 --> 00:13:45.990
She teaches violin to students
at home on weekdays.

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:48.740
What are you? A walking
wiki for Iketeru-kun?

00:13:49.910 --> 00:13:54.410
Beer! Beer! Beer, now!

00:13:54.410 --> 00:13:57.830
We didn't have to choose the day Iketeru
Oniisan isn't around to go get a drink.

00:13:57.830 --> 00:14:00.250
I can't help that he isn't here.

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:05.670
"Izakaya"

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:05.670
Where did that love for your co-workers
that you passionately spoke of go?

00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:07.590
"Green Room
for Uramichi Omota-sama"

00:14:10.550 --> 00:14:14.980
Uramichi Oniisan. I'm sorry for causing
you guys so much trouble yesterday.

00:14:14.980 --> 00:14:18.190
That's okay, but you should
knock first, okay?

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:22.650
What?

00:14:22.650 --> 00:14:25.780
From now on, I'll try my best
to manage my physical condition

00:14:25.780 --> 00:14:28.410
as a working adult, and... um...

00:14:28.410 --> 00:14:31.580
Hey, don't read your notes.

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:32.830
Iketeru Oniisan.

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:33.870
Hm?

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:37.620
You don't have to try so hard...

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:39.920
...for someone else's sake.

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:42.920
Uramichi Oniisan...

00:14:44.420 --> 00:14:46.420
What in the world...

00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:48.720
Iketeru Oniisan.

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:49.970
What?

00:14:51.350 --> 00:14:53.600
"Mitsuo Kumatani"

00:14:56.930 --> 00:14:59.020
Um... Kumatani-san.

00:14:59.020 --> 00:15:01.020
Ah, yes?

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:02.310
Are you okay?

00:15:02.310 --> 00:15:03.690
I'm okay. I'm okay.

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:05.610
Um... I'm Iketeru.

00:15:05.610 --> 00:15:07.320
Yeah, I know!

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:09.950
Your voice is so hoarse!

00:15:09.950 --> 00:15:11.410
I let my guard down.

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:15.870
Tell Derekida-san and the other higher-ups
that I'll get better right away!

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:20.210
It's a costumed role. It'll work out okay
if a staff member gets inside it for you.

00:15:20.210 --> 00:15:21.210
Yeah.

00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:23.460
Hey, guys!

00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:26.630
<i>Together with Maman </i>without Kumao-kun?!

00:15:26.630 --> 00:15:31.010
There's no point in doing a show
that works out okay like that, is there?!

00:15:31.010 --> 00:15:33.640
Once again, she's turned into
that mysterious character.

00:15:33.640 --> 00:15:37.270
You're just getting carried away,
aren't you? We all know that.

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:41.350
Children are not like us
damn dead-beat adults.

00:15:41.350 --> 00:15:42.900
Damn adults, seriously...?

00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:48.440
They have a rich and sharp sensitivity,
and we entertain such children.

00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:51.360
If we put a random person in that costume,

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:54.120
they'll know immediately!

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:58.870
We work more closely with
Kumao-kun than the staff does.

00:15:58.870 --> 00:16:05.090
Meaning, we, the cast members, should
know his gestures and habits better!

00:16:05.090 --> 00:16:10.090
Especially you, Usao-kun. You lived in the
same dorm room with him during college!

00:16:10.090 --> 00:16:13.680
So you should feel the strongest
sense of duty, this time.

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:18.770
What? I don't feel like
I'm that close to him.

00:16:18.770 --> 00:16:22.350
"Just watching"

00:16:18.770 --> 00:16:22.350
Has this farce become a routine?

00:16:22.350 --> 00:16:23.690
"Just watching"

00:16:22.350 --> 00:16:23.690
Who knows...

00:16:25.190 --> 00:16:29.070
I agree with what Utano Oneesan said.

00:16:29.070 --> 00:16:33.610
Are you playing along?
Or are you being serious?

00:16:33.610 --> 00:16:36.910
Utano Oneesan is shocked
that you took her seriously

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:39.240
when she was just kidding around!

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:41.120
So that Kumatani-san won't feel sad...

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:42.660
Well, I won't feel sad or anything.

00:16:42.660 --> 00:16:45.210
...we should do the things we can do
with everything we've got.

00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:48.460
It's possible that he
might've caught my cold, so...

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:51.670
Ah...

00:16:53.050 --> 00:16:55.180
"Omota"

00:16:55.180 --> 00:16:56.260
"Omota"

00:16:55.180 --> 00:16:56.260
Hm?

00:16:56.260 --> 00:16:57.430
Hi.

00:16:57.430 --> 00:17:01.930
Sorry! I totally forgot
and went to the gym!

00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:04.020
It was cold waiting outside
all this time, wasn't it?

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:05.810
It wasn't bad at all.

00:17:05.810 --> 00:17:07.020
Anyway, here.

00:17:07.020 --> 00:17:10.190
"Man-Eating Salmon
vs.
Bunny on a Moped"

00:17:07.020 --> 00:17:10.190
The DVD I was talking about.

00:17:10.190 --> 00:17:11.650
Thanks.

00:17:11.650 --> 00:17:13.200
Don't catch a cold, okay?

00:17:17.740 --> 00:17:20.330
That... might've done it.

00:17:22.750 --> 00:17:24.580
"Mud Boat"
"Izakaya"
"Beer"

00:17:26.580 --> 00:17:30.380
You're asking me why
I'm so obsessed with marriage?

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:33.800
Because people keep asking me,
"Why aren't you getting married?"

00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:36.470
and I started feeling distressed.

00:17:36.470 --> 00:17:38.890
I-It may not look it,

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:40.760
but when I was in my 20s,

00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:44.940
I didn't intend to become
a dull 30-something woman,

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:47.060
who'd be obsessed with marriage.

00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:50.940
Hey! It's your fault!
Why'd you have to ask that?!

00:17:50.940 --> 00:17:53.440
But I wonder why...

00:17:53.440 --> 00:17:57.200
I don't know why, but I'm becoming
like that person without knowing it...

00:17:57.200 --> 00:18:01.950
Someone who I used to look
down on when I was young...

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:03.370
--Ouch!
--I can't be the ideal me,
like I imagined myself being.

00:18:03.370 --> 00:18:06.170
--It hurts! It's stretching.
It's stretching and it hurts.
--I can't be the ideal me,
like I imagined myself being.

00:18:06.170 --> 00:18:09.540
--It hurts! It's stretching.
It's stretching and it hurts.
--I'm getting pulled into "normal"
and I have no energy left

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:13.380
to fight the "natural" thing
forced on me, either.

00:18:13.380 --> 00:18:16.220
Anyway, it's hard to live!

00:18:19.010 --> 00:18:20.930
Ah! I'm sorry!

00:18:20.930 --> 00:18:24.930
It's no problem.
It's a little cold, that's all.

00:18:24.930 --> 00:18:28.560
More like a big problem
with all that I spilled on you.

00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:29.400
I'm really sorry.

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:33.190
"Izakaya"

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:33.190
It was that idiot's fault
for asking you a stupid question.

00:18:33.190 --> 00:18:35.650
"Izakaya"

00:18:33.190 --> 00:18:35.650
What? Me?

00:18:39.410 --> 00:18:42.660
I wonder... if that did it...

00:18:42.660 --> 00:18:45.540
Ah...

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:48.080
Uramichi-san! There's snow! Snow!

00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:50.790
There's a lot of snow on the ground here!

00:18:50.790 --> 00:18:52.790
Let's have a snowball fight!

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:53.670
No.

00:18:53.670 --> 00:18:54.670
Take this!

00:18:55.010 --> 00:18:58.430
"Private Property"

00:19:04.600 --> 00:19:05.470
There!

00:19:05.470 --> 00:19:06.430
It's cold!

00:19:06.430 --> 00:19:07.430
Usahara, you bastard!

00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:10.150
It's your own fault for
not paying attention, idiot!

00:19:12.110 --> 00:19:13.730
A direct hit!

00:19:17.360 --> 00:19:18.950
That must be it.

00:19:21.450 --> 00:19:25.450
Let's try harder together
today for Kumatani's sake!

00:19:25.450 --> 00:19:27.120
Let's do it!

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:30.870
"Mitsuo Kumatani"

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:30.870
Don't worry, Kumatani. I'll do my best!

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:35.380
"Mitsuo Kumatani"

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:35.380
He's right, Kumao-kun!
We'll be a little different today!

00:19:35.380 --> 00:19:35.920
"Mitsuo Kumatani"

00:19:35.380 --> 00:19:35.920
Well...

00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:38.920
"Man-Eating Salmon
vs.
Bunny on a Moped"

00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:38.920
...you're actually stressing me out.

00:19:39.630 --> 00:19:41.640
Hey, kids!

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:44.890
Usao-kun came to play
with you today again!

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:47.390
Let's play together, hop!

00:19:49.270 --> 00:19:50.940
Where's Kumao-kun?

00:19:51.980 --> 00:19:56.360
To tell you the truth,
Kumao-kun had a fight with Usao-kun.

00:19:56.360 --> 00:19:59.150
That's why they couldn't
come here together.

00:19:59.150 --> 00:20:00.240
I don't like it!

00:20:00.240 --> 00:20:01.570
Where is Kumao-kun?

00:20:01.570 --> 00:20:03.370
I want Kumao-kun!

00:20:03.370 --> 00:20:06.370
Isn't Usao-kun the one who should go away?

00:20:15.130 --> 00:20:16.420
I can't take it anymore!

00:20:16.420 --> 00:20:20.340
Kumatani is the only one popular
among women and children!

00:20:20.340 --> 00:20:24.090
Look back on your own
behavior before crying about it.

00:20:24.090 --> 00:20:29.390
If my behavior is so bad that it leaks
through the costume, it's hopeless!

00:20:29.390 --> 00:20:31.390
Then... well...

00:20:31.390 --> 00:20:33.100
...wear this, for now.

00:20:33.100 --> 00:20:34.440
What?

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:37.860
I'm going to wear... Kumao...?

00:20:37.860 --> 00:20:41.360
Kids want to see Kumao-kun, so...

00:20:41.360 --> 00:20:45.950
S-So you make light of me,
too, Uramichi-san.

00:20:45.950 --> 00:20:48.790
Have I ever respected you?

00:20:48.790 --> 00:20:50.950
Come to think of it, no.

00:20:50.950 --> 00:20:54.290
If I do my best and play Kumao,
will I be respected?

00:20:54.290 --> 00:20:55.790
Not by me.

00:20:55.790 --> 00:20:57.880
I see.

00:20:57.880 --> 00:21:02.010
Kids! Kumao-kun came for you!

00:21:02.010 --> 00:21:03.720
Yay! Kumao-kun!

00:21:03.720 --> 00:21:05.590
It's Kumao-kun!

00:21:05.590 --> 00:21:11.230
Now, it's time for the fun ABC Exercise!

00:21:11.230 --> 00:21:13.560
Wait...

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:16.100
Is it really Kumao-kun?

00:21:19.400 --> 00:21:22.030
Isn't this Kumao-kun kind of tall?

00:21:22.030 --> 00:21:27.370
Yeah... And his movement...
is kind of annoying, isn't it?

00:21:28.950 --> 00:21:30.240
Who are you?

00:21:36.250 --> 00:21:40.250
No, no, no...! They're sharp!
They're too sharp!

00:21:40.250 --> 00:21:42.970
How did you get found out
when you're wearing the costume?

00:21:42.970 --> 00:21:44.130
I can't take it anymore.

00:21:44.130 --> 00:21:45.380
When you're wearing the costume...

00:21:45.380 --> 00:21:47.800
Stop saying that.

00:21:47.800 --> 00:21:51.270
I'll be honest and tell them
that Kumao-kun can't come today

00:21:51.270 --> 00:21:52.980
because he's sick.

00:21:54.770 --> 00:21:57.770
Kids! There's something
I want to tell you!

00:21:57.770 --> 00:21:59.020
What?!

00:21:59.020 --> 00:22:01.110
He's got Usao-kun's head...

00:22:01.110 --> 00:22:02.730
...but his body is Kumao-kun's?!

00:22:02.730 --> 00:22:04.780
Hop...

00:22:04.780 --> 00:22:06.030
Oh... crap...

00:22:06.030 --> 00:22:08.030
Usao-kun?

00:22:08.030 --> 00:22:09.370
Yes, sir!

00:23:39.870 --> 00:23:40.870
"Wanna Quit Bunny"

00:23:40.870 --> 00:23:44.880
"Wanna Quit Bunny"

00:23:40.870 --> 00:23:44.880
Kumatani... I really can't
live without you.

00:23:44.880 --> 00:23:47.590
"Wanna Quit Bunny"

00:23:44.880 --> 00:23:47.590
Huh? What's with you?
You're creeping me out.

00:23:47.590 --> 00:23:51.590
"Wanna Quit Bunny"

00:23:47.590 --> 00:23:51.590
Um... I'm so grateful I have you.

00:23:51.590 --> 00:23:52.890
"Wanna Quit Bunny"

00:23:51.590 --> 00:23:52.890
What?

00:23:52.890 --> 00:23:54.560
"Wanna Quit Bunny"

00:23:52.890 --> 00:23:54.560
He hung up on me.
